OneTimeUseIdPolicy::checkAction
├── given the configId was never initialized
│   └── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED
├── given the pinned id is unburned
│   └── it should return VALIDATION_SUCCESS
├── given the pinned id has been burned
│   └── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED
├── given the burn happened in an earlier transaction
│   └── it should still return VALIDATION_FAILED
├── given the pinned id is shared with another action slot
│   └── when that id is burned
│       └── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED from every slot pinned to it
├── given a batch of many executions in one settlement
│   └── it should return VALIDATION_SUCCESS for every one of them while unburned
├── it should never itself burn the id
├── given the call targets this policy with calldata shorter than a selector
│   └── it should fail closed and return VALIDATION_FAILED
├── given the call targets this policy and the selector is consume
│   ├── when the id argument is this session's OWN id
│   │   └── it should return VALIDATION_SUCCESS
│   ├── when the id argument names ANOTHER session's id
│   │   └── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED
│   └── when the calldata is malformed (shorter than an id argument)
│       └── it should fail closed and return VALIDATION_FAILED
├── given the call targets this policy and the selector is consumeFor
│   ├── when the id argument is this session's OWN id
│   │   └── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED
│   └── when the id argument names ANOTHER session's id
│       └── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED
└── given the call is unrelated to this policy
    └── it should return VALIDATION_SUCCESS
